course: dictionary
lesson: 10734
title: Upright: standing straight and good
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Upright is one of these words. Most of the time it means standing or sitting straight up, not lying down or leaning. «Keep the bottle upright so the juice does not spill.» The clue is spill: the bottle must stay straight up, or the juice runs out.
explain: Upright can also describe a person. «Her grandad was an upright man who always told the truth.» Nobody is shaped like a bottle here, so upright must mean honest and good. Always ask: does the meaning fit this sentence, or do I need another meaning?
explain: Upright can be a thing too. «The goalkeeper leaned against one of the uprights.» An upright is a post that stands straight up, like the side posts of a goal. Read the words around the word, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Upright means standing or sitting straight up, not lying down or leaning.
fact: «Bolt upright» means suddenly very straight, as in «she sat bolt upright in bed».
fact: An upright person is honest and good, and an upright piano is a tall piano that stands against a wall.
fact: In maths and science, upright means vertical: at a right angle to the ground.
exercise: «Keep the bottle upright so the juice does not spill.» What does upright mean here? | *Standing straight up, not tipped over | Lying flat on its side | Empty and light | Shaking hard
exercise: «Her grandad was an upright man who always told the truth.» What does upright mean in this sentence? | *Honest and good | Standing tall | Sleeping | Bent over
exercise: «The goalkeeper leaned against one of the uprights.» What is an upright in this sentence? | A player's shirt | A small gate | A ball kicked high into the air | *A post that stands straight up
test: «Sit upright in your seat when the car is moving.» Why do we sit upright in a car? | To make the car go faster | To look out of the window | *To sit safely and properly | To sleep better
test: «Real bears can walk a few steps upright, but it is slow and awkward.» What does upright mean in this sentence? | Lying down | Running very fast | Hidden in the trees | *Standing up on two legs
exam: Which word could replace upright in «Sit ___ in your chair»? | Crooked | Lazy | Bent | *Straight
